            <span>How can I actually check my IQ level online?</span>
            <span class="ml-4 shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 flex items-center justify-center text-zinc-500 group-hover:text-zinc-900 dark:group-hover:text-white transition-colors">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm sm:text-base text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed pt-3 border-t border-zinc-200/60 dark:border-zinc-800/60">
            You can take our standardized 20-minute cognitive assessment or 10-minute quick screening directly in your browser. Both tests assess non-verbal fluid reasoning and pattern induction, computing an estimated deviation IQ score and population percentile with instant results and no paywalls.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-2xl sm:rounded-3xl p-5 sm:p-7 bg-zinc-50/50 dark:bg-zinc-900/40 transition-all open:bg-zinc-50 dark:open:bg-zinc-900/70 shadow-2xs">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none font-heading font-bold text-lg sm:text-xl text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">
            <span>Can you increase your IQ score?</span>
            <span class="ml-4 shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 flex items-center justify-center text-zinc-500 group-hover:text-zinc-900 dark:group-hover:text-white transition-colors">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm sm:text-base text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed pt-3 border-t border-zinc-200/60 dark:border-zinc-800/60">
            While fundamental biological fluid intelligence is largely genetically stable, your operational performance on IQ tests can improve significantly. Familiarity with matrix transformation rules, cognitive drills (like N-back and mental rotation), high sleep quality, stress management, and test pacing help eliminate unforced errors and unlock your highest natural score.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-2xl sm:rounded-3xl p-5 sm:p-7 bg-zinc-50/50 dark:bg-zinc-900/40 transition-all open:bg-zinc-50 dark:open:bg-zinc-900/70 shadow-2xs">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none font-heading font-bold text-lg sm:text-xl text-zinc-950 dark:text-white">
            <span>What are IQ tests primarily used for today?</span>
            <span class="ml-4 shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 flex items-center justify-center text-zinc-500 group-hover:text-zinc-900 dark:group-hover:text-white transition-colors">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm sm:text-base text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed pt-3 border-t border-zinc-200/60 dark:border-zinc-800/60">
            In clinical and educational settings, standardized IQ batteries (such as the WAIS-IV and WISC-V) are used to diagnose learning differences, assess cognitive recovery following neurological injury, identify gifted learners, and analyze specific cognitive strengths and weaknesses across working memory, perceptual reasoning, and processing speed.
          </p>
        </details>
